he power $(8)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116241/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2463ef2-c276-53cb-a1a1-8601789574d3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116241"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-116229/selection/98bafb703e8881681adce0bc8183cfd2e95c4591cd3a7132eb4a51d89a40e205" :answer/id #uuid "f44a0b38-313f-5ab1-9533-31d35c6569a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All real numbers" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116229/selection/9428b228a91978b57bbd43ebbcd93d67ef456f0b613ee71b26de106a78b2c2ed" :answer/id #uuid "7a3a0c65-a723-5f5a-919b-9dcd7da0c4f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116229/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer/id #uuid "fae32e94-8fa3-5478-a92e-c76d4a412773" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No solution" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116229/selection/0ffcd15795e34096849b65562b63d39d444e2d6511f2bdba60b68039c64a76f9" :answer/id #uuid "cfe895a1-284b-5961-b31f-07dbddfbc847" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116229/selection/434e5b9ed40adaf3ca2255268857c0c63681f364c2d21459ddbc2c544571b271" :answer/id #uuid "bd5fc4fb-2330-51cc-b8d5-b9dc712008be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge -4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-116229/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26d77f55-8a43-53f4-9a83-43bcb18a6f17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-116229/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" :answer-field/choices ["q-116229/selection/98bafb703e8881681adce0bc8183cfd2e95c4591cd3a7132eb4a51d89a40e205" "q-116229/selection/9428b228a91978b57bbd43ebbcd93d67ef456f0b613ee71b26de106a78b2c2ed" "q-116229/selection/6d6811ceb4fb69a54ce1b24e6804e5f0148bafa1b76b847b06436eb966d36b67" "q-116229/selection/0ffcd15795e34096849b65562b63d39d444e2d6511f2bdba60b68039c64a76f9" "q-116229/selection/434e5b9ed40adaf3ca2255268857c0c63681f364c2d21459ddbc2c544571b271"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-116229" :question/id #uuid "2eba8e28-81e4-514d-9e97-b76a4ae28edc" :question/math-academy-id "q-116229" :question/problem "Solve $(4x-5)^{4}+25\\le 9.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the quartic term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4x-5)^{4}+25 & \\le 9 \\\\ (4x-5)^{4} & \\le -16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(4x-5)^{4}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(4)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-116229/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2463ef2-c276-53cb-a1a1-8601789574d3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116229"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7651"] :question/problem "Solve the inequality $2(x - 2)^3 - 5 \\gt      11.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-2)^{3}-5 & >11 \\\\ 2(x-2)^{3} & >16 \\\\ (x-2)^{3} & >8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the cube root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(x-2)^{3}} & >\\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\ x-2 & >2 \\\\ x & >4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7653"] :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(5x + 2)^4}{9} - 3 \\gt 6.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the quartic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5x+2)^{4}}{9}-3 & >6 \\\\ \\frac{(5x+2)^{4}}{9} & >9 \\\\ (5x+2)^{4} & >81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the fourth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{(5x+2)^{4}} & >\\sqrt[4]{81} \\\\ |5x+2| & >3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n5x + 2 \\lt -3 \\qquad \\textrm{or} \\qquad 5x + 2 \\gt 3\n$$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2 & <-3 &  &  & 5x+2 & >3 \\\\ 5x & <-5 &  &  & 5x & >1 \\\\ x & <-1 &  &  & x & >\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\lt -1 \\quad \\textrm{or} \\quad x \\gt \\dfrac{1}{5}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7652"] :question/problem "Solve $(5x-1)^6 + 5 \\geq -4.$" :question/worked-solution "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5x-1)^{6}+5 & \\ge -4 \\\\ (5x-1)^{6} & \\ge -9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $(5x - 1)^{6} \\geq 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(6)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the given inequality is all real numbers." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
